  "description": "Standalone timer nodes for FluxFlow: interval and cron-schedule sources plus delay, throttle, and debounce transforms over an injected TimeProvider, with broadcast output/error/event ports. No engine required.",
  "id": "FluxFlow.Components.Timers",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-19T12:53:12.403Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "AQC/WEPABwEzafoZvldWRHwPsUwMi/dQBPL5bD181l8jvhavRAQrbOUkYyjGNS2Ek9irddQgUO/uoiIDe7Ws/Q==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 58666,
  "published": "2026-06-19T12:50:34.15Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt on the FluxFlow.Nodes kit: timer.interval and timer.schedule are FlowSource<T> sources (started via StartAsync, ticks minted as FlowMessage envelopes), and timer.delay/throttle/debounce are FlowNode<TInput, TInput> transforms that preserve the message correlation id and time off the injected TimeProvider. The engine factories, module, registration extensions, design-metadata provider, the definition-options reader, and the string-to-Type resolution layer are removed; each node takes its settings record and TimeProvider directly and depends only on FluxFlow.Nodes (runs without the engine).",
